---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/benchmarks.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const { ci, builds, targets } = data;
---

<Base title="Benchmarks" description="Fennec's real benchmark numbers against Rust twins, measured in CI. In progress.">
  <section class="wrap head">
    <span class="pill">In progress</span>
    <h1>Benchmarks</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every kernel is a Fennec program and a Rust twin doing the same work, the idiomatic way. These are real numbers from CI, and they
      aren't where we want them yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Speed against Rust</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Today's only native engine is the JIT, whose target is {targets.jit}% of Rust's speed. Release builds, with a target of {targets.release}%,
      don't exist yet.
    </p>
    <div class="table">
      <div class="tr th">
        <span>Kernel</span><span class="num">Rust</span><span class="num">Fennec JIT</span><span>Speed vs Rust</span>
      </div>
      {
        ci.kernels.map((kernel) => (
          <div class="tr">
            <span class="name">{kernel.name}</span>
            <span class="num">{kernel.rust_ms.toFixed(1)} ms</span>
            <span class="num">{kernel.fennec_ms.toFixed(1)} ms</span>
            <span class="bar-cell">
              <span class="track">
                <span class="fill" style={`width: ${kernel.percent}%`} />
                <span class="target" style={`left: ${targets.jit}%`} title={`JIT target: ${targets.jit}%`} />
              </span>
              <strong>{kernel.percent.toFixed(0)}%</strong>
            </span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      No kernel meets the {targets.jit}% target in this run. Medians of repeated runs, from commit <code>{ci.commit}</code> on {ci.date}, on {ci.machine}.
      The line on each bar marks the target. A shared CI machine is noisy, so these move by several percent between runs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Build and test times</h2>
    <p class="note">Measured on {builds.machine}, at commit <code>{builds.commit}</code>, on {builds.kit}.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><strong>{builds.one_function_s} s</strong><span>to rebuild after changing one function</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>{builds.first_s.toFixed(0)} s</strong><span>for its first build, with an empty cache. We want this much lower.</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>&lt;{builds.tests_unchanged_s} s</strong><span>to rerun tests when nothing they depend on changed, on one small test file</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>How it's measured</h2>
    <p>
      Both sides run on the same machine, taking turns, and must print the same result. The Rust twin is built with
      <code>-C opt-level=3 -C target-cpu=native</code>. A failure is fixed in the compiler, never by changing the benchmark. The kernels and the
      method are in <a href="https://github.com/fennec-language/fennec/tree/main/bench">the repository</a>, and you can{' '}
      <a href={`${base}speed/`}>read how the two speeds are designed</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .head {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 3.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .tr {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 2.2fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .tr:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .th {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .num {
    text-align: right;
  }

  .bar-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .bar-cell strong {
    width: 2.75rem;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .track {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-bright);
  }

  .target {
    position: absolute;
    top: -4px;
    bottom: -4px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--text);
  }

  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .stat {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .stat strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .stat span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tr {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
    }

    .th {
      display: none;
    }

    .tr .num {
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .name,
    .bar-cell {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
